<Project>

  <!-- =====================================================================
       Build settings shared by the three reference layers
       (DynamicPatcher, PatcherYRpp, Extension).

       These are .NET Framework 4.8 projects, so building them needs the v4.8
       reference assemblies. Install them once with the Visual Studio Installer
       (Individual components):
           .NET Framework 4.8 SDK
           .NET Framework 4.8 Targeting Pack
       which places them at
           C:\Program Files (x86)\Reference Assemblies\Microsoft\Framework\.NETFramework\v4.8

       History, so this is not "simplified" back into the same trap:

       Before the targeting pack was installed, the build was pointed at the
       copy inside the NuGet package Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies
       (via TargetFrameworkRootPath / FrameworkPathOverride + explicit HintPaths
       + netstandard from the package's Facades folder). That reduced the errors
       from 73 to 6, but could not finish: MSBuild resolved an IMPLICIT
       System.Core through the {AssemblyFolders} search path and found a
       leftover v3.5 developer pack, giving
           System.Core 3.5.0.0  next to  mscorlib 4.0
       which defines Action/Func twice (CS0433) and breaks
       IDynamicMetaObjectProvider (CS7069).

       With the official targeting pack present, the normal resolution finds
       v4.8 first and none of that workaround is needed. If the pack is ever
       missing again, that is the symptom to expect - install the pack rather
       than reintroducing the package-based override.

       Keep this file ASCII-only: Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a UTF-8 file with
       no BOM as ANSI and non-ASCII text turns into mojibake.
       ===================================================================== -->

</Project>
